keenable.snippet:
Slepian–Wolf coding [11], of which DISCUS [9] is a classical construction, lets a decoder with side information recover a source from fewer bits than the source alone would need.

a lossless, tag-verified protocol in which the sender runs no model and holds no table at run time, and a language-model receiver reconstructs the message by hash-pruned beam search, with a negative acknowledgement and a fallback that deliver every message (Section 2);

With a NACK and a raw fallback, a sender that only computes hashes delivers every message, losslessly and verified by a tag, while a receiver with a language model does the modelling. Measured against an in-domain classical sender, it does not pay on our pre-registered endpoint: it spends 18.4 bits more per message than PPM order 1.

